cloud-architecture-diagram

direction right
typeface clean
styleMode shadow
colorMode pastel

Services [label: "Domain Services", color: green] {
  Catalog [label: "Catalog and Pricing"]
  Checkout [label: "Checkout and Orders"]
  Inventory [label: "Inventory"]
}

SystemOfRecord [label: "Authoritative State", color: purple] {
  PostgreSQL [icon: aws-rds, label: "RDS PostgreSQL - System of Record"]
}

EventPublishing [label: "Reliable Event Publishing", color: yellow] {
  Outbox [label: "Transactional Outbox"]
  Relay [label: "Outbox Relay"]
  EventBridge [icon: aws-eventbridge, label: "EventBridge"]
}

Queues [label: "Consumer Buffers", color: orange] {
  SearchQueue [icon: aws-simple-queue-service, label: "Search Index Queue"]
  FulfilmentQueue [icon: aws-simple-queue-service, label: "Fulfilment Queue"]
  NotificationQueue [icon: aws-simple-queue-service, label: "Notification Queue"]
  AnalyticsQueue [icon: aws-simple-queue-service, label: "Analytics Queue"]
}

DerivedState [label: "Derived and Ephemeral State", color: blue] {
  Search [icon: aws-opensearch-service, label: "OpenSearch Derived Index"]
  Cache [icon: aws-elasticache, label: "Valkey Cache"]
}

ExternalConsumers [label: "External Consumers", color: gray] {
  ERP [label: "ERP and Warehouse"]
  Notifications [label: "Messaging Providers"]
  Analytics [label: "Analytics Platform"]
}

Catalog > PostgreSQL: Catalog truth
Checkout > PostgreSQL: Orders and payment state
Inventory > PostgreSQL: Inventory and reservations

Catalog > Cache: Cache aside reads
Checkout > Cache: Safe ephemeral data

PostgreSQL > Outbox: Commit state and event together
Outbox > Relay: Read committed events
Relay > EventBridge: Publish domain events

EventBridge > SearchQueue: Route search events
EventBridge > FulfilmentQueue: Route fulfilment events
EventBridge > NotificationQueue: Route notification events
EventBridge > AnalyticsQueue: Route analytics events

SearchQueue > Search: Idempotent indexing
FulfilmentQueue > ERP: Asynchronous integration
NotificationQueue > Notifications: Asynchronous delivery
AnalyticsQueue > Analytics: Asynchronous events

legend [position: bottom-left] {
  [color: purple, label: "Authoritative state"]
  [color: blue, label: "Derived or ephemeral state"]
  [connection: -->, label: "Request or event"]
}
